    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Honda Click For Beginners Hanoi: Selection Guide</h1>
    <p>The Honda Click is one of the easiest motorbikes to learn on in Hanoi, and it earns that reputation on three points: a low seat, a light frame and a fully automatic transmission. For a first-time rider, those three qualities remove most of the stress that a manual bike or a heavy scooter would add to an already demanding city. The Click also sits in our standard automatic class next to the Yamaha Mio, at 150,000 VND per day, and you can collect it from our shop at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, any day between 09:00 and 21:00. This guide walks through how to decide whether the Click is the right first machine for you.</p>
    <p>It lives inside our wider <a href="/hanoi-scooter-rental/">Hanoi scooter rental</a> hub, where the full automatic fleet and its guides are collected, and the verified numbers behind every model and tier are laid out on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> page. If your stay in the city runs longer than a few weeks, the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental in Hanoi</a> plan usually works out cheaper than paying day by day, so read it before you commit to a tier.</p>
<nav class="toc"><ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Why the Click suits first-time riders</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">Seat height, weight and control feel</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">Learning the automatic twist and go</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">Click versus Yamaha Mio for beginners</a></li>
